From 1aa2df8bf0d630f5998d6e841ff5bf6324b958f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <yaeger.james42@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:41:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(library): public skills catalog, MCP servers and custom
 tools per account

Add a Library to SwarmAgents so a user can give their agent more
capabilities: browse a public catalog of 2,584 real skills from 14 verified
public repositories, import a skill from a GitHub URL, a zip archive or the
in-app editor, add MCP servers from the verified connector catalog or the
public MCP registry, and add custom tools (including tools the agent writes
for itself).

- every import is staged first: the user reviews the SKILL.md, the file list
  and the scripts before the "untrusted content - review the scripts" notice
  lets the install through
- zip uploads are read by a defensive reader (zip slip, absolute paths,
  symlinks, zip64, zip bombs, entry/size caps); a skill is capped at 200
  files, 4 MB in total, 1 MB per file
- everything is per account: the state lives in the account directory, the
  MCP credentials are sealed with AES-256-GCM and are never returned to the
  browser or logged
- a role can only reference skills and servers the account really installed
- installed skills are synced into the user's VM (/workspace/.claude/skills)
  so the Claude Code worker picks them up, the MCP servers are wired into
  the run's --mcp-config and the custom tools run through a small MCP server
  inside that VM - never in the Next.js process
- the catalog index is generated by scripts/build-skills-index.ts, which
  walks the SKILL.md files of the real repositories; the tool library index
  comes from the official MCP registry
