+### The library (skills, MCP servers, tools)
+
+The **Library** drawer (the "Library" button in the role bar) is where a user
+gives their agent more capabilities. Everything in it is **per account** and
+everything it installs **runs inside that user's own VM** — never in the
+Next.js process, never on the host.
+
+| Tab | What it does |
+| --- | --- |
+| Skills | Browse the public skill catalog, import a skill from a GitHub URL, upload a zip or write one in the editor, review it, install it and assign it to a role. |
+| MCP servers | Browse the verified connector catalog and the public MCP tool library, or add your own endpoint. Credentials are stored encrypted and are never sent back to the browser. |
+| Tools | Add a custom tool (a script that runs in your VM). The agent can also write one for itself. |
+
+**The skill catalog** (`lib/library/catalog/skills-index.json`) is generated by
+`scripts/build-skills-index.ts`, which walks the `SKILL.md` files of verified
+public repositories (`lib/library/catalog/skill-sources.json` — Anthropic's own
+skills, Cloudflare, Google, Supabase, Microsoft, GitHub's awesome-copilot and
+several well-known community collections) and records the name, description,
+source URL, license and file list of every skill it finds. Nothing in the
+catalog is invented: an entry exists only when a `SKILL.md` with that name and
+description was really in the repository. `scripts/build-tools-index.ts` does
+the same for the public tool library (the official MCP registry plus the
+verified connector catalog).
+
+**The Agent Skills format** is a folder with a `SKILL.md`: YAML frontmatter
+(`name` + `description`, optionally `license`, `version`, `allowed-tools`)
+followed by a markdown body, plus optional `scripts/`, `references/` and
+`assets/` folders. `lib/library/skills/format.ts` parses and validates it.
+
+**Every import is staged first.** The user sees the `SKILL.md`, the file list,
+the scripts it would run and an "untrusted content — review the scripts"
+warning before anything is installed (`POST /api/library/skills/import` returns
+the preview, `POST /api/library/skills/install` commits it).
+
+**Caps and hardening**
+
+- Zip uploads are read by a defensive reader (`lib/library/skills/zip.ts`):
+  path traversal ("zip slip"), absolute paths, symlinks, encrypted entries,
+  zip64, too many entries, oversized files, oversized archives and zip bombs
+  (expansion ratio) are all refused.
+- A skill is capped at 200 files, 4 MB in total, 1 MB per file and 256 KB for
+  the `SKILL.md` itself.
+- The role editor only ever offers skills and servers the account really
+  installed, and a role can never reference more than the account allows.
+
+**How a skill reaches the agent.** Before a run starts, the skills assigned to
+the role are written into the user's VM at
+`/workspace/.claude/skills/<skill>/…`, where Claude Code picks them up as
+project skills. The MCP servers of the account are wired into the run's
+`--mcp-config` (with their secrets injected inside the VM), and the custom
+tools are exposed through a small MCP server the app writes into the VM
+(`/workspace/.swarm/library/tools.mjs`). A tool the agent writes for itself
+lands in `/workspace/.swarm/agent-tools/<name>/tool.mjs` and is harvested back
+into the account's library when the run ends.
+
+Library API (all per account, all behind the session gate):
+
+| Route | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `GET /api/library` | The account's skills, MCP servers, tools and role assignments. |
+| `GET /api/library/catalog?type=skills\|tools\|connectors&q=…` | Browse/search the public catalogs. |
+| `POST /api/library/skills/import` | Stage an import (catalog, URL, zip or editor) and get the preview back. |
+| `POST /api/library/skills/install` | Install a staged import. |
+| `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/library/skills/<id>` | Read, flag (reviewed/trusted) or remove an installed skill. |
+| `GET/POST /api/library/mcp`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/library/mcp/<id>` | Manage MCP servers (secrets are write-only). |
+| `GET/POST /api/library/tools`, `DELETE /api/library/tools/<id>` | Manage custom tools. |
+| `GET/POST /api/library/assignments` | Per-role assignments of skills, servers and tools. |
+
 ### Local sign-in (login / signup)
 
 SwarmAgents ships with a small local password auth layer (`lib/auth.ts` +
